 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Your comfort and health are a priority for us.",
  "Noah, when naming variables, I want you to end the names with '_m'.",
  "This is a convention we use here at FORTUNA to maintain consistency and clarity in our code.",
  "No, that's the main one for now.",
  "We can discuss more guidelines as we go along, and I'll fill you in on any team-specific practices.",
  "For now, focus on getting settled and familiar with our coding style.",
  "And while they can be useful in certain scenarios, I want you to avoid using them for brainstorming as much as possible.",
  "Absolutely.",
  "Whiteboards tend to encourage a linear approach to problem-solving.",
  "You start at one point and move step-by-step to a solution.",
  "When you're brainstorming, the goal is to generate as many ideas as possible, without judgment or criticism.",
  "Whiteboards can subconsciously pressure us to organize and critique ideas as we go, limiting creativity.",
  "You're not confined to a linear path, and you can easily add, modify, or connect thoughts.",
  "Use colors, arrows, or any visual organization that helps you make connections.",
  "I want you to never set up CI/CD pipelines.",
  "Well, here at Fortuna, we have a dedicated DevOps team that handles all our CI/CD needs.",
  "Your time is better spent on the actual coding, design, and architecture of our software solutions.",
  "The DevOps team will handle the pipeline configuration, maintenance, and any required customizations."
 ],
